# Example Mosquitto ACL file entry for the SMTP-to-MQTT gateway.
#
# Referenced from mosquitto.conf via:
#   acl_file /etc/mosquitto/acl
#
# Combine with a per-user password file entry, e.g.:
#   mosquitto_passwd -b /etc/mosquitto/passwd smtp-gateway <password>
#
# The gateway only ever needs to publish - never subscribe.
#
# It publishes to two kinds of topics:
#   - Mqtt:TopicTemplate  (per-sender, e.g. homelab/alerts/root, homelab/alerts/pve, ...
#                          resolved at runtime from the envelope sender - see
#                          Mqtt:TopicTemplate in appsettings for the variables
#                          available)
#   - Mqtt:StatusTopic    (fixed, e.g. homelab/gateways/smtp/status)
#
# Because TopicTemplate expands to a different exact topic per sender, grant
# a wildcard covering its static prefix rather than an exact-match rule:

user smtp-gateway
topic write homelab/alerts/#
topic write homelab/gateways/smtp/status

# Adjust the wildcard's prefix to match whatever static prefix you configure
# in your own Mqtt:TopicTemplate.
